1. Ethical Considerations — biases & mitigation (writeup to include)

Bias sources:

MNIST: If your training/test split accidentally includes digit styles dominated by some writers (e.g., digits from specific writers in train only), model may overfit handwriting styles.

Amazon Reviews: Brand representation bias (some brands over-represented), demographic bias in reviewers, sarcasm or domain misinterpretation.

Consequences:

Wrong predictions disproportionately impacting certain user groups; mischaracterized sentiment harming product decisions.

Mitigation tools & approaches:

TensorFlow Fairness Indicators: use dataset slices (e.g., by reviewer country, product category) to check fairness metrics across slices.

Data balancing / re-sampling: ensure diverse representation when training.

Model explainability: SHAP or saliency maps for CNNs, LIME for text models, to detect unfair decision patterns.

Human-in-the-loop: manual review for flagged predictions.

spaCy rule-based systems: use an EntityRuler + manual rules to reduce false positives for brands; annotate corner cases and retrain or expand patterns.

