2. Troubleshooting Challenge — common TensorFlow bugs + fixes

Dimension mismatch:

Error: ValueError: Shapes (None, 10) and (None, 1) are incompatible

Fix: Ensure your loss matches labels: use sparse_categorical_crossentropy with integer labels or categorical_crossentropy with one-hot labels. Or convert labels with to_categorical.

Incorrect activation/loss:

For multi-class classification use softmax on final layer + categorical_crossentropy.

Model not learning / low accuracy:

Learning rate too high/low — try Adam with default or tune; add BatchNormalization; reduce dropout.

GPU out-of-memory:

Reduce batch_size or use smaller model.

Shape errors with Conv2D:

Check input shape: Keras expects (height, width, channels). For grayscale set channels=1.

"fetch first" / push-to-repo confusion — unrelated to TF, but for git merges: ensure you resolve merge conflicts in code files (the merge message issue you saw earlier).

